diff --git a/.shipwright/agent_docs/architecture.md b/.shipwright/agent_docs/architecture.md
index 9d9179cd..601a0d48 100644
--- a/.shipwright/agent_docs/architecture.md
+++ b/.shipwright/agent_docs/architecture.md
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@ Two features are pure consumers of producer-owned files under `<project>/.shipwr
 - **Triage Tab** — read consumer + status-flip producer over `triage.jsonl` (ADR-101/106). Five `/api/triage/*` endpoints (`counts`, `:projectId` list, `promote`/`dismiss`/`snooze`). The list is a TS port of `shared/scripts/triage.py read_all_items` (last-status-wins, **record-boundary recovering**, Python-fixture-parity-gated), reading the **union tracked ∪ gitignored `triage.outbox.jsonl`** with status flips residence-derived (ADR-166) and each item annotated `pendingDelivery` (ADR-169) + `campaignSlug`/`campaignStatus`. Promote is a cross-store transaction (idempotent retry + orphan-promote guard); a 5 s mtime cache fronts reads; per-project fault isolation via `Promise.allSettled`. **Fix now** copies the producer `launchPayload` (`stripControlChars` byte-port; ADR-116) to the clipboard — never a server launch (rule 1); **Start Campaign** performs the `draft → active` write (§6). All fields render as plain text (XSS-safe). The Triage Detail modal additionally recognizes file-path-like tokens in `evidencePath` and free-text `detail` (`lib/extractFileMentions.ts`, regex-based, no I/O) and renders them as `FileLink`s; clicking one opens `TriageFilePanel` as a second column beside the existing detail column (widened `Dialog.Content`, not a second overlay), reusing the already path-guarded `SmartViewer` — read-only, no new write surface.
 - **Compliance Grade** — read-only observer of `compliance/dashboard.md` (FR-01.43); the WebUI never writes it. `core/compliance-reader.ts` (`parseDashboard`, pure + fixture-tested) extracts the badge fields and slices the "Control Verdict" + "CI Security" markdown sections (excluding the dead-in-browser artifacts links). `GET /api/external/projects/:projectId/compliance` (`external/compliance/routes.ts`, mounted read-only; `{status: missing|invalid}` on graceful absence) feeds `lib/complianceApi.ts` + `useProjectCompliance` (30 s poll, `retry:false`). `ComplianceGradeBadge` (A→emerald / B→amber / ≤C→red) renders on the Projects table and the single-project board header; clicking opens `ComplianceDetailModal` (Radix Dialog), whose body renders the two slices via `DocumentMarkdown` (react-markdown + remark-gfm) 1:1 with the dashboard.
 - **Ship's-Log Documents panel** — read-only observer curating four groups of a project's own docs (FR-01.60, iterate-2026-08-31-shipslog-documents-panel): Requirements (per planning-section `spec.md`, dynamically discovered), Iterate mini-specs (flat `.shipwright/planning/iterate/*.md`, search-filterable), and a fixed 5-row Agent Docs / Compliance curation each (skip-if-missing, no error row). `core/shipslog-docs-reader.ts` (pure fs reader, `pathGuard`+`realPathGuard` on every path even though none is client-supplied) backs `GET /api/external/projects/:projectId/shipslog-docs` (`external/shipslog-docs/routes.ts`); `ShipsLogDocumentsPanel.tsx` + `ShipsLogSpecsTabs.tsx` (`@radix-ui/react-tabs`) + `ShipsLogDocList.tsx` render it as the Ship's-Log page's new right column (2fr:1fr grid, `ShipsLogPage.tsx`), each row opening the existing `SmartViewerModal`. No new write surface — but it DID surface and fix a latent gap in an existing one: `SmartViewer.tsx`'s Edit-button gating (§6's `PUT /file`) was coupled to the `popOut` prop, so a modal-nested viewer (`SmartViewerModal`, `TriageFilePanel`) never showed Edit; `onSaved` is now always wired, decoupling Edit from pop-out (only the "Pop out" affordance itself stays non-recursive). `MarkdownEditorBanners.tsx` also gained a global "saved to disk only, not committed" notice across every `MarkdownEditorModal` use.
-- **Codex model catalog** — a global (not project-scoped) read-only observer of the Codex CLI's own model catalog (iterate-2026-09-19-codex-model-catalog, follow-up to shipwright#471/#473). `core/codex-models-probe.ts` shells out to `codex debug models` via the same `defaultRunShim` win32-`.cmd`-shim pattern `readiness-probe.ts` already uses for `codex --version` (needs no auth — verified empirically), filters to `visibility==="list"` entries whose `slug` also passes the existing `CODEX_MODEL_SLUG_PATTERN` gate, and discards the large per-model payload (reasoning-level metadata, multi-KB prompt text) before it ever leaves the server. `GET /api/codex-models` (`routes/codex-models.ts`) wraps this in its own in-memory TTL cache (5 min success / 30 s failure, deliberately separate from readiness's own cache lifetime) and always returns HTTP 200 with `status: ok|stale|unavailable` — never blocking the launch form. `ModelTierOverrideFields.tsx`'s three Codex model fields (Implementation model, Plan review, Review) consume it via `useCodexModels()` (called unconditionally to satisfy the rules of hooks; the *fetch* is gated on `runtime === "codex"`) as a shared `<datalist>` combobox, free text always still accepted. No new persisted state (in-memory cache only, lost on restart) and no change to server-side launch validation.
+- **Codex model catalog** — a global (not project-scoped) read-only observer of the Codex CLI's own model catalog (iterate-2026-09-19-codex-model-catalog, follow-up to shipwright#471/#473). `core/codex-models-probe.ts` shells out to `codex debug models` via the same `defaultRunShim` win32-`.cmd`-shim pattern `readiness-probe.ts` already uses for `codex --version` (needs no auth — verified empirically), filters to `visibility==="list"` entries whose `slug` also passes the existing `CODEX_MODEL_SLUG_PATTERN` gate, and discards the large per-model payload (reasoning-level metadata, multi-KB prompt text) before it ever leaves the server. `GET /api/codex-models` (`routes/codex-models.ts`) wraps this in its own in-memory TTL cache (5 min success / 30 s failure, deliberately separate from readiness's own cache lifetime) and always returns HTTP 200 with `status: ok|stale|unavailable` — never blocking the launch form. `ModelTierOverrideFields.tsx`'s two Codex model fields (Plan review, Review — the former Implementation-model field was removed, iterate-2026-09-26-codex-model-field-removal) consume it via `useCodexModels()` (called unconditionally to satisfy the rules of hooks; the *fetch* is gated on `runtime === "codex"`) as a shared `<datalist>` combobox, free text always still accepted. No new persisted state (in-memory cache only, lost on restart) and no change to server-side launch validation.
 
